            <div xml:id="d864">

                <pb facs="0949" n="939" xml:id="pg939"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–1648: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-12-16">December 16, 1948</date>.<lb/>[Received December
                        18—1:29 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>555. Peiping, south (Nankuan) airfield was subjected Communist artillery fire 9
                    a.m. today whereupon 7 of 8 CNAC and CAT planes on field immediately took off
                    only one remaining presumably for VIPS. Chartered plane <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Staul</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic">St. Paul</hi>] arriving 10 a.m. was
                    therefore signalled off and failed to pick up second load of day.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 811, Department 555, Shanghai 542, Tsingtao, Tientsin.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
